<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Matthias von der Schulenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1661">1661</a>–<a href="/years/1747">1747</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Matthias von der Schulenburg was a German soldier who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and other powers before becoming field marshal of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1715. In 1716 he commanded the defence of Corfu against a large Ottoman army and fleet, which abandoned the siege after weeks of assaults. The Venetians erected a statue to him on the island during his lifetime, and he spent his later years in Venice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-matthias-von-der-schulenburg.jpg" alt="Johann Matthias von der Schulenburg" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Ritratto_di_Johann_Matthias_von_der_Schulenburg_-_Antonio_Guardi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
